      "reasoning": "All seven current answers agree with their own captured worked solutions and the earlier mathematical conclusions. q-177648: since 0 belongs to I, the intersection is contained in X_0={0}×[0,1]; this segment also belongs to every X_i, establishing equality. Option 3 and the source image depict the same closed segment. q-181303: the source uses N={1,2,...}, so R×N is the family of full horizontal lines at positive integer heights. Option 1 and the source image represent this same infinite family with different numbers of visible sample lines. q-73951: the last two component equations force x_1=-2 and x_2=3, but their first component is 4 instead of 3, so there is no solution. q-73952: coefficients (-3,4) produce (-7,-1,6), giving sum 1. q-105168: coefficients (-7,1,6) produce (2,1,2), giving sum 0. q-73992: coefficients (2,3,-2) produce (-5,-10,1), giving sum 3. q-34058: b=2a_1+a_2=(1,1,7), so b belongs to the span and the coefficient product is 2. No captured grade is supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions.",
